 "title": "Nobody",
 "dates": "Monday, November 30 – Sunday, December 6, 2009",
 "logline": "A week of strange hours: a blowout nobody stays for, a speech about thirty thousand, a drive with no destination — and on the one night he’s where he said he’d be, somebody comes to check.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Your father said the guest says grace, and Theo said it. Then Nonna asked if his mother prays for him. “Da stasera, io.”",
   "if": "theo_said_grace"
  },
  {
   "text": "At Trumbull your brother watched Theo work the vending machines. “You can quit buying. I already like you.”",
   "if": "theo_met_danny"
  },
  {
   "text": "Two in the morning, your father’s basement: *tell me what you think about. be specific.* You typed: *the car door. your hands in my jacket. how you made it slow on purpose.* And you kept going.",
   "if": "e18_text==\"reckless\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Then she called. Nearly three hours on the porch in Nonna’s afghan. She fell asleep in the middle of the Madonna.",
   "if": "skye_called"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sunday, at the cannoli, on Theo’s phone: *Jack Costigan and Skye Callender are now friends.* He turned it face down and passed you the box.",
   "if": "theo_knows_skye_jack"
  },
  {
   "text": "At Sully’s, Lena asked who you were texting. “No one.”",
   "if": "skye_texting"
  }
 ],
